WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:04.770
- I don't think any other
stock has captivated investors

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:08.830
on Wall Street or Main
Street the way Tesla has.

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:11.710
It's just become one of the
most controversial names

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:14.960
and one of the most
watched names out there.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:18.300
This summer, Tesla became the
most valuable auto company

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:19.360
in the world,

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:21.800
surpassing Toyota and
claiming a market cap

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:26.180
of nearly $183 billion
before continuing its climb.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:29.040
- The electric vehicle maker's
stock speeding this year.

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:30.680
- Musk's wealth skyrocketing

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.700
thanks to a surge in Tesla shares,

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.480
making him wealthier than Warren Buffet.

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:36.940
- But the company's fundamentals

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:39.140
don't seem to explain the rise.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:42.580
For example, Toyota sold
almost 25 times as many

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:45.030
vehicles as Tesla did last year.

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:48.300
Instead, the rally has been
driven by investor enthusiasm

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.540
for CEO Elon Musk.

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:52.491
In a belief by some that in the future,

00:00:52.491 --> 00:00:55.320
cars everywhere will be
powered by batteries,

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:56.400
not gasoline.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.058
Here's how Tesla became the
most valuable auto maker

00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:00.413
in the world.

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:05.470
Tesla developed its first
car in the early 2000s.

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:07.300
But to follow its ballooning share price,

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.460
a good place to start is last fall.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:13.930
In October 2019, Tesla
reported a surprise profit

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:15.340
for its latest quarter,

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:18.120
and that just sent its shares soaring.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:20.230
Just a few months prior,

00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:24.060
Tesla shares were hovering
near a three year low.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:25.899
The prior year, Elon Musk had tweeted

00:01:25.899 --> 00:01:30.899
that he was going to take
Tesla private at $420 a share.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:34.360
And that landed him in the
cross hairs of regulators.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.410
He also kind of had a history
of missing financial targets

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:39.030
and car delivery targets.

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:41.440
So that's why this surprise earning spree

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:42.850
was a really big deal.

00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:44.834
Amid the rush of investor optimism,

00:01:44.834 --> 00:01:48.170
in mid-November Musk held
an event in Los Angeles

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:50.530
to reveal Tesla's Cybertruck.

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:53.103
What he did was he
unveiled this pickup truck

00:01:53.103 --> 00:01:56.080
that looked unlike any other pickup truck

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:57.430
we had ever seen before,

00:01:57.430 --> 00:02:01.340
and he boasted that it was
really, really durable.

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:03.400
At the event, a Tesla employee

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:06.250
threw a metal ball at the
window to show its strength

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:08.319
but ended up breaking the glass.

00:02:08.319 --> 00:02:10.380
- I should say also, we're
going to be offering rides

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:11.454
in this all night.

00:02:11.454 --> 00:02:14.287
(audience cheers)

00:02:16.613 --> 00:02:18.169
Yeah, don't mind the glass.

00:02:18.169 --> 00:02:19.377
(audience laughs)

00:02:19.377 --> 00:02:22.276
- The next day, shares
fell more than six percent,

00:02:22.276 --> 00:02:24.540
but amid press around the event,

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:26.290
the stock quickly recovered,

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:30.920
and on December 23, it surged past $420.

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:33.690
The reason that 420 mark
is kind of a milestone

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:36.530
is that, you know, that
was kind of the tweet

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:39.400
that landed Musk in the
cross hairs of regulators.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:41.040
The SEC later said the tweet

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:42.730
was a reference to marijuana culture

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:44.800
that Musk used to amuse his girlfriend.

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:47.320
The shares crossing 420 later in the year,

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:49.360
it was kind of a victory in that sense.

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:52.270
In the following weeks,
Tesla had a string of wins.

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:54.340
The company said it met its delivery goal

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:57.240
of 360,000 cars for the year.

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:59.180
And less than a year after breaking ground

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:00.570
at its China plant,

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:03.200
the car maker met its objective
for Model 3 production

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:04.150
at the facility,

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:06.760
and held a press conference
to celebrate deliveries

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:10.120
of China-made Model 3s
to Chinese customers.

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:13.639
Many people viewed China as
the world's biggest market

00:03:13.639 --> 00:03:15.130
for electric vehicles,

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:18.340
so in order for Tesla to make this journey

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:22.329
from a small start-up to a global behemoth

00:03:22.329 --> 00:03:24.312
producing electric cars,

00:03:24.312 --> 00:03:27.970
Polish investors say that it
needs to target that market.

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:31.270
So this boosted expectations
for the coming year.

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:34.242
The investor momentum
continued when on January 29,

00:03:34.242 --> 00:03:37.760
Tesla posted a profit for
the second quarter in a row.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:38.980
On the earnings call,

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:40.560
the company said it was well on its way

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:42.390
to producing its next car,

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:45.560
the Model Y compact sport utility vehicle.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:47.980
And it told investors the
business should be profitable

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:49.310
going forward.

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:52.380
So this was around the
time that Tesla shares

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:54.810
really just started to go parabolic,

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:57.880
and you saw Wall Street
investors, Main Street investors,

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:02.700
kind of all piling into
Tesla shares, Tesla options,

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:04.647
and it just kind of
became this huge frenzy

00:04:04.647 --> 00:04:06.470
around the company.

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:09.400
But not everyone was
betting for the car company.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:12.120
The fascinating thing about Tesla is that

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:16.380
despite its meteoric rise in
the stock market this year,

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:19.740
it remains one of the most popular shorts,

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:22.820
so that means it's a really
popular bet for investors

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:26.150
who think the shares are
going to absolutely plummet.

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:27.370
When the stock goes up,

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:29.450
that's painful for a short investor.

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:31.290
That means that they're losing money.

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:32.830
So some people can't hold on

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:35.210
to these money-losing
positions for too long,

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:37.290
so they have to close out their position,

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:40.400
and sometimes they do that
by buying Tesla stock.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:41.919
In this kind of unusual twist,

00:04:41.919 --> 00:04:46.780
you have investors who think
the shares are going to go down

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:49.770
actually helping to drive it up.

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:52.688
But the stock run-off was
stopped short in March.

00:04:52.688 --> 00:04:54.800
Despite investor enthusiasm,

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:56.900
Tesla was not immune to the market effects

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:59.250
of the Coronavirus lockdowns.

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:02.270
That month, California
issued stay-at-home orders,

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:05.090
leading Tesla to suspend
production at a factory,

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:06.840
and interrupting the company's ramp-up

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:08.700
for its newest vehicle.

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:10.797
The stock fell in March and
then quickly bounced back

00:05:10.797 --> 00:05:13.230
as the market started to recover.

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:14.412
At the heart of this downturn,

00:05:14.412 --> 00:05:17.300
the federal reserve enacted
a massive stimulus plan

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:18.750
to buoy the economy,

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:21.070
fueling a broader recovery
in the stock market

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:23.530
that also lifted stocks like Tesla.

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:26.800
On April 29, Tesla
reported another profit,

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:27.970
the third in a row.

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:30.660
Even through the low of the S&amp;P 500,

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:33.740
the S&amp;P was down roughly
30 percent year to date,

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:35.830
and meanwhile, even
through that time frame,

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:37.030
Tesla stock was up.

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:39.040
So despite a recession,

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:42.990
a global pandemic that
could crimp demand for cars,

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:46.120
Tesla's stock has still
been resilient this year.

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:49.500
Then on June 10, investors
pushed the auto makers' stock

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:52.490
past $1,000 a share for
the first time ever.

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:55.044
After Musk told employees it
was time to begin production

00:05:55.044 --> 00:05:58.670
on the company's all
electric semi-trailer truck.

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:02.260
By July, Tesla became the
world's most valuable car maker,

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:03.930
overtaking Toyota,

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:06.850
and on the 2nd, Musk
taunted the short sellers

00:06:06.850 --> 00:06:10.219
when shares opened above
$1,200 for the first time

00:06:10.219 --> 00:06:12.763
after Tesla deliveries beat expectations

00:06:12.763 --> 00:06:15.640
and investors anticipated
the company's inclusion

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:17.960
in the S&amp;P 500 Index.

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:20.200
In order to be considered for the S&amp;P 500,

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:22.830
a company needs to deliver
a cumulative profit

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:24.327
over four consecutive quarters,

00:06:24.327 --> 00:06:26.370
including the most recent.

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:29.950
So even before Tesla's most
recent earnings report,

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:32.053
a ton of investors were anticipating,

00:06:32.053 --> 00:06:34.800
hey we think it's going to
be profitable this quarter,

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:36.730
we think it's going to be in the S&amp;P 500,

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:39.700
and that drove the stock even higher.

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:41.970
On an earnings call on July 22,

00:06:41.970 --> 00:06:44.300
Tesla said it hit that goal,

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:47.940
defying the Wall Street
bears who expected a loss.

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:49.030
- We were able to achieve

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:51.563
a fourth consecutive profitable quarter,

00:06:51.563 --> 00:06:54.670
and although the automotive
industry was down

00:06:54.670 --> 00:06:57.388
about 30% year over year in
the first half of the year,

00:06:57.388 --> 00:06:59.128
we managed to grow deliveries

00:06:59.128 --> 00:07:00.520
in the first half of the year.

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:04.760
- If you bought 10 shares of
Tesla last June, in June 2019,

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:08.910
it would have cost you a
little more than $1,700.

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:12.120
If you held on to that
investment through late July,

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:15.960
it would have been
worth more than $15,000.

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:18.530
Bears still say that the
stock is going to go down.

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:21.960
They don't think that Tesla
will bring electric vehicles

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:22.973
to the masses.

